# Rust
target/

# colcon / ROS 2 build products (regenerable from src/)
build/
install/
log/
libdatachannel-install/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# data/ is NOT ignored, on purpose. Those .png/.npy frames are the only copy of
# the scene a measurement was taken in -- ADR 0004's baseline says "re-run on the
# same frames", and on 2026-08-18 a directory outside this workspace vanished
# between two commands. 179 MB against 393 GB free is not a reason to risk them.
# When a measurement stops referencing an observation dir, `git rm -r` it in the
# commit that supersedes the measurement, so the pruning has a stated reason.
